      "claim": "The closest analogue, 7-(2-hydroxyethyl)-1,3-dimethylxanthine (etofylline), had an absolute oral bioavailability of 93.4±6.3% in children, directly showing that N7-substituted 1,3-dimethylxanthines can be essentially completely absorbed.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
