    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C26"],
      "claim": "Pentoxifylline, an N1-alkylated xanthine with a 5-oxohexyl side chain, has low absolute bioavailability (~28%) in humans, showing that some N-alkyl xanthines undergo substantial first-pass loss; however, its side chain is at N1 and its similarity to the query is lower.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is doxofylline, an N7-(1,3-dioxolan-2-ylmethyl)-1,3-dimethylxanthine. The closest analogue etofylline (N7-hydroxyethyl) has 93.4% absolute oral bioavailability, and caffeine/theophylline with the same 1,3-dimethylxanthine core are essentially 100% bioavailable. Low-F xanthines such as pentoxifylline and lisofylline carry N1 side chains and are less transferable. Therefore F >= 20% is strongly supported; predict high.",
